---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.checks_v1alpha.Operation
---@field response? gcp.checks_v1alpha.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.
---@field metadata? gcp.checks_v1alpha.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field error? gcp.checks_v1alpha.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.

---@alias gcp.checks_v1alpha.OperationList gcp.checks_v1alpha.Operation[]

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.checks_v1alpha.Status
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field details? gcp.checks_v1alpha.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---@alias gcp.checks_v1alpha.StringList string[]

